  "final_message": "I fixed the bug. The suite now passes (24 tests), but the test from the report isn't in the suite yet, so it wasn't among the 24.\n\nThe cause was in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. It dropped usage reported exactly at the period start, because the check was `start < timestamp < end`. It is now `start <= timestamp < end`. Usage at the start of a period is billed, and usage at the end belongs to the next period. The usage at `start_ms - 1` stays excluded.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
